From f9e611f5db2ef6fd8c323933eb5155278bfb892a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 12:54:39 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] perf(kanban): reuse read-only board connections for
 linked-card reads [daveey]

The Desktop's linked-card endpoint opened a fresh sqlite connection to every
board and every sync replica on each call (~16 files): schema parse, WAL-index
setup and close cost ~2.5 ms a file, so one chat's cards took ~40 ms median
with 120-340 ms tails, over the phase 5 budget of 40 ms.

cached_ro() keeps one read-only connection per file in the long-lived
dashboard process, shared across the threadpool behind a per-connection lock,
reopened when the file's inode changes (a rebuilt replica) or after any
sqlite error. Idle autocommit readers hold no snapshot, so writers and
TRUNCATE checkpoints are unaffected. _read_session_tasks and replica_cards use
it. Live laptop data: 1.3-1.8 ms median per chat (was 40-42 ms), 40 chats
4.6 ms (was 43.7 ms), same cards.

Tests: reuse + fresh commits, reopen on replace, drop on error, missing file
never created, checkpoint not blocked, 8-thread sharing, and replica_cards
seeing a link added and one released after the first read.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
